From d9e356431e058b7dd62fb568832bffefdca5a8ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:39:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tests: SubjectAltName support in the openssl
 CertificateGenerator

The GHSA-vvx9 tests generate certificates with DNS, SRV, URI and IP
SANs. 7.2's CertificateGenerator.inc cannot add SANs and leaves the
digest to the OpenSSL config default. This brings the generator of later
branches: SHA-256 (accepted at security level 2), SAN support through a
temporary config file, and bug68265/bug68879/san_peer_matching on
generated certificates instead of the stored .pem files (deleted). Test
change only.

Backport of php-src 52c2f1126d, c7fe71c8b7 and 21a2da2349 (Nikita
Popov), Sury's 7.2 patches 0201-0203, with his 0209 (no trailing comma
in calls for 7.2).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
